A||N||4||Zorba||V8 fiero question||||1||
Z||000000||Zorba||10-29-2000||03:04 PM||||For you guys with v8 fieros, what did you use for throttle cable - original? - and what did you use for a throttle cable bracket. The original cable seems to long and I am having a hard time findin the right bracket for it. Thanks for any assistance.||||reg||1
Z||000001||V8Fiero||10-29-2000||04:35 PM||||I used the original cable with a custom made bracket. Made one out of cardboard for a template and had a buddy of mine weld one up. Works great and cheap too.......<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000002||cowans||10-30-2000||03:03 PM||||Zorba, I used the Cable Mount Bracket of a 1984 Chev Beauville 305 with the 1985 fiero gt throttle cable. ....fit PERFECTLY to a 4bbl Rochester....Note: my F40/fiero chassis is extended 7". Sandy ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Zorba||10-30-2000||10:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cowans:<BR><B>Zorba, I used the Cable Mount Bracket of a 1984 Chev Beauville 305 with the 1985 fiero gt throttle cable. ....fit PERFECTLY to a 4bbl Rochester....Note: my F40/fiero chassis is extended 7". Sandy </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So far I am experimenting with attaching the longer 4cylinder throttle cable to a chev cable, thru some maneuvering inside the engine bay...seems to be working...but if not, I will follow your lead on teh beauville...I hope auto\zone has them in stock... <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Zorba||10-31-2000||04:12 AM|||| Answering my own original question: a $13.99 bracket from checker auto parts and the original cable did the trick. Very minor modification to the cable bracket using a pair of plyers. No brainer.||||reg||1
